        "en": "Nima said the whole problem with possessive endings: kombim (my boiler), sözleşmem (my contract), randevum (my appointment). Tolga Bey's answer shows the case endings: “Sözleşmeyi bugün notere götürüyorum!”: -yi marks the thing he takes, -e where he takes it. One noun, many endings: noter, notere, noterde, noterden.",
